    // Each warp handles WMMA_M=16 rows; we have WARPS_M*WMMA_M=64 rows total
    // Use all threads: one warp per row block, 8 warps cover 64 rows total
    // Assign rows to threads: thread tid handles row (tid / (BN/32))
    // Actually: use warp-per-row approach for BN=128 (4 warps per row)
    // Alternative simpler: each thread handles one or more complete rows sequentially
